knowledge_statements.statement_latex:
If \(C\subset\mathbb{R}^n\) is fully amenable at \(\bar x\), then \(C\) is parabolically derivable at \(\bar x\) for every \(w\in T_C(\bar x)\) and parabolically regular at \(\bar x\) for every \(v\in N_C(\bar x)\). For every \(w\in T_C(\bar x)\), the second-order tangent set \(T_C^2(\bar x\mid w)\) is nonempty and polyhedral, and
\[
\sigma_{T_C^2(\bar x\mid w)}(v)=
\begin{cases}
-d^2\delta_C(\bar x\mid v)(w),&v\in N_C(\bar x)\text{ and }v\perp w,\\
+\infty,&\text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]

